"Farming changed people's lives, and not only for the better. A field can feed more people than the same land left wild, and the number of people grew. But in most places that have been studied, skeletons show that people became shorter as farming took hold, a sign of poorer food or more sickness. Stored grain could be owned, and the gap between richer and poorer families widened. A farmer is also tied to the field. When a harvest failed, it was much harder to move away.": "2c41c4a55b74",
